---
params: [title: String, root: String, description: String, markdown: String, content: String]
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title><%= title %></title>
    <meta name="description" content="<%= description %>">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:opsz,wght@9..144,300..700&family=Plus+Jakarta+Sans:wght@400..700&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500;600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="<%== root %>assets/style.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="<%== root %>assets/oops.css">
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/markdown" href="<%= markdown %>">
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="<%== root %>icon.png">
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="top">
      <div class="wrap top-inner">
        <a class="brand" href="<%== root %>index.html">kex</a>
        <span class="brand-sub">oops</span>
        <span class="spacer"></span>
        <a class="back" href="https://docs.kex.run">docs ↗</a>
        <a class="back" href="https://kex.run">kex.run ↗</a>
      </div>
    </header>
    <div class="wrap">
      <main class="content prose">
<%== content %>
      </main>
    </div>
    <footer class="machine">
      <div class="wrap">
        <p><strong>Reading this with a program or a language model?</strong> Every page here is also plain Markdown. <a href="/llms.txt"><code>/llms.txt</code></a> explains the codes and links each one's Markdown, <code>/&lt;CODE&gt;.md</code> is one code (<a href="<%= markdown %>">this page</a>), <a href="/llms-full.txt"><code>/llms-full.txt</code></a> is every code with its explanation in one file, and <a href="/registry.json"><code>/registry.json</code></a> is the compiler's own <code>kex --explain all --json</code>.</p>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
